# A glob merges its files' schemas by name. `country` is only in February, so it comes after
# the columns of January (the first file). `props` is a JSON object: it has no DataScript type in
# M1 (M2-03), so it can only be projected. `**` matches any number of directories.
mode: check
show: schema
---- query
from '../../data/events/*.ndjson' | take 1;
from '../../data/**/2024-0?.ndjson' | take 1;
from '../../data/events/*.ndjson' | where props == 'x'
---- expected
error[DS2008]: column `props` has a type DataScript cannot use yet
  --> query:3:43
  |
3 | from '../../data/events/*.ndjson' | where props == 'x'
  |                                           ^^^^^ this column is `Struct("page": Utf8, "ref": Utf8)` in Arrow
  |
  = help: it can only be projected as it is: `project props`, `project-away props`
  = note: column `props` was read from ../../data/events/*.ndjson
  = note: nested, JSON and GUID columns become `dynamic` and `guid` values in M2

query 1 columns:
  ts: string
  user: string
  event: string
  duration_ms: long
  props: (error)
  country: string

query 2 columns:
  ts: string
  user: string
  event: string
  duration_ms: long
  props: (error)
  country: string

query 3 columns:
  ts: string
  user: string
  event: string
  duration_ms: long
  props: (error)
  country: string
